NAME
       test, [ - evaluate a conditional expression

SYNOPSIS
       test expression
       [ expression ]

DESCRIPTION
       Exits 0 if EXPRESSION is true and 1 if it is false. When invoked
       as [ the last argument must be ].

FILE TESTS
       -e F   F exists
       -f F   F is a regular file
       -d F   F is a directory
       -r F   F is readable
       -x F   F is executable
       -s F   F exists and is not empty

STRING TESTS
       -z S   S is empty
       -n S   S is not empty
       S = T  strings are equal
       S != T strings differ

NUMERIC TESTS
       -eq -ne -lt -le -gt -ge

COMBINING
       -a     and
       -o     or
       !      negate

EXAMPLES
       test -f /etc/shell && echo present
       [ "$n" -gt 10 ] && echo big

SEE ALSO
       expr(1), csh(1)
